{"diagnosis": "mem_la_addr low bits are 2'b10 instead of 2'b00, causing the fetch misalign trap with low bits nonzero and FAIL 0xdead. Expected word-aligned fetches with low bits 2'b00. Root cause is line 382 building both fetch ({next_pc[31:2]+mem_la_firstword_xfer,2'b10}) and data ({reg_op1[31:2],2'b10}) addresses with forced 2'b10.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -382,1 +382,1 @@
-	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b10} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b10};
+	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b00} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b00};", "expected": "tohost PASS 0x1 with no TRAP: fetch misalign"}

